@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@token = REPLACE_WITH_A_REAL_TOKEN
@tokenNoDeleteScope = REPLACE_WITH_A_TOKEN_MISSING_DELETE_SCOPE
@tokenExcludedDeck = REPLACE_WITH_A_TOKEN_THAT_EXCLUDES_deckId_BELOW
@tokenNoSchemaDelete = REPLACE_WITH_A_TOKEN_ON_A_ROLE_WITH_canDelete_FALSE

### =========================================================================
### SETUP — root deck to hold the test cards (copy the returned id into @deckId)
### =========================================================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "DeleteCardTestDeck"
}

###
@deckId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### SETUP — plain text card to delete in the basic-success scenario (copy id into @cardId)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "CardToDelete",
  "parentId": "{{deckId}}",
  "fieldType": "text"
}

###
@cardId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### =========================================================================
### 1) SUCCESS — delete an existing card → 204 No Content, empty body
### =========================================================================
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card/{{cardId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 2) Delete the SAME card again → 404 NOT_FOUND (already gone)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card/{{cardId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3) Delete a non-UUID cardId → 404 NOT_FOUND (isUuid guard, never a raw DB error)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card/not-a-uuid
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4) Delete a well-formed UUID that never existed → 404 NOT_FOUND
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card/11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5) Delete a DECK id passed as if it were a cardId → 404 NOT_FOUND
### (the lookup filters nodes.type = 'field', so a container id never matches)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card/{{deckId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### =========================================================================
### 6) AUTH — missing Authorization header → 401 UNAUTHORIZED
### =========================================================================
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card/{{cardId}}

### 7) AUTH — malformed/unknown token → 401 UNAUTHORIZED
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card/{{cardId}}
Authorization: Bearer this-token-does-not-exist

### =========================================================================
### 8) SCOPE — token has no "delete" scope → 403 FORBIDDEN
### Generate @tokenNoDeleteScope in Settings → API with scope = ["read","write","update"]
### =========================================================================
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card/{{cardId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenNoDeleteScope}}

### =========================================================================
### 9) TOKEN POLICY — deckId (the card's parent) is in the token's excluded list → 403 FORBIDDEN
### Generate @tokenExcludedDeck in Settings → API excluding {{deckId}} explicitly
### =========================================================================
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card/{{cardId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenExcludedDeck}}

### =========================================================================
### 10) ROLE — token's role has schema canDelete = false → 403 FORBIDDEN
### Generate @tokenNoSchemaDelete on a role whose Settings → Roles schema
### permissions have "Delete card/deck" unchecked for this project
### =========================================================================
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card/{{cardId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenNoSchemaDelete}}

### =========================================================================
### 11) MEDIA CLEANUP — delete an image card that real records reference:
### the media row gets purged (storage file + DB row) and the field is
### stripped from every record that had it set. Full flow below.
### =========================================================================

### 11a) create the image card WITH a base64 default (uploads real media)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "FotoConMedia",
  "parentId": "{{deckId}}",
  "fieldType": "image",
  "config": {
    "base64": "iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAAAEAAAABCAQAAAC1HAwCAAAAC0lEQVR42mNk+A8AAQUBAScY42YAAAAASUVORK5CYII=",
    "mimeType": "image/png",
    "filename": "foto.png"
  }
}

###
@mediaCardId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@mediaId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
### (copy fieldType card's "id" into @mediaCardId and its config.defaultMediaId into @mediaId from the 11a response)

### 11b) create a record on the root deck referencing that media by id
### (the deck's slug is its simpleName, from the DeleteCardTestDeck setup step: deletecardtestdeck)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/deletecardtestdeck
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "FotoConMedia": "{{mediaId}}"
}

### 11c) delete the card — purges the referenced media and clears the field from the record above
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/card/{{mediaCardId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 11d) verify: GET the deck's records — FotoConMedia should now be absent/null on every row
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/deletecardtestdeck
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### =========================================================================
### CLEANUP — remove the test deck itself (cascades the remaining test cards/records)
### =========================================================================
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/table/{{deckId}}?cascade=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
